### Register a new player
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "charlie", "password": "password123"}

### Register the same name again → 409 USERNAME_TAKEN
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "charlie", "password": "password123"}

### Bad input → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "c!", "password": "short"}

### Login OK → token
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "charlie", "password": "password123"}

### Wrong password → 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "charlie", "password": "wrongpass1"}

### Unknown user → also 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS (same message!)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "nobody", "password": "password123"}

### Login and save the token
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "charlie", "password": "password123"}

> {%
    client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### My wallet: WITH token → 200
GET http://localhost:8080/api/wallet/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### My wallet: NO token → 401 UNAUTHORIZED
GET http://localhost:8080/api/wallet/me

### My wallet: FAKE token → 401 TOKEN_INVALID
GET http://localhost:8080/api/wallet/me
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiIxIn0.fakesignature

### My profile → 200
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Old URL is gone, even WITH a token → 404
GET http://localhost:8080/api/wallet/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ===== DUPLICATE LOGIN =====

### Device A logs in
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "charlie", "password": "password123"}

> {%
    client.global.set("tokenA", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### Device A works → 200
GET http://localhost:8080/api/wallet/me
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}

### Device B logs in with the SAME account
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "charlie", "password": "password123"}

> {%
    client.global.set("tokenB", response.body.accessToken);
    client.global.set("refreshB", response.body.refreshToken);
%}

### Device A is kicked → 401 KICKED
GET http://localhost:8080/api/wallet/me
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}

> {%
    client.test("Device A is kicked", () => {
        client.assert(response.status === 401, "Expected 401 but got " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.code === "KICKED", "Expected KICKED");
    });
%}

### Device B works → 200
GET http://localhost:8080/api/wallet/me
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenB}}

### ===== REFRESH + ROTATION =====

### Refresh → new access + new refresh token
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{"refreshToken": "{{refreshB}}"}

> {%
    client.global.set("usedRefresh", client.global.get("refreshB"));
    client.global.set("refreshB", response.body.refreshToken);
    client.global.set("tokenB", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### The new access token works → 200
GET http://localhost:8080/api/wallet/me
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenB}}

### Reusing the OLD refresh token → 401 REFRESH_INVALID (rotation!)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{"refreshToken": "{{usedRefresh}}"}

### ===== LOGOUT =====

### Logout → 204
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{"refreshToken": "{{refreshB}}"}

> {%
    client.test("Logout returns 204", () => {
        client.assert(response.status === 204, "Expected 204 but got " + response.status);
    });
%}

### After logout, the access token stops working → 401
GET http://localhost:8080/api/wallet/me
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenB}}

### After logout, refresh fails → 401 REFRESH_INVALID
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{"refreshToken": "{{refreshB}}"}